│ patch_name               │ symmetry_shared_ry_crx_ring_hub                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ A completely different, more parameter-efficient, symmetry-aware ansatz that preserves    │
│                          │ the fixed training setup but reorganizes the trainable parameters to improve              │
│                          │ generalization and convergence. The new ANSATZ_SPEC uses:                                 │
│                          │ - a 3-way pre-RZ scheme (corners, edges, center) with shared parameters to exploit        │
│                          │ tic-tac-toe rotational symmetry                                                           │
│                          │ - a single global RY parameter applied to all qubits (dramatically reducing parameter     │
│                          │ count)                                                                                    │
│                          │ - ring entanglement on the outer perimeter via alternating CRX gates (two ring            │
│                          │ parameters) to capture rotational structure with few parameters                           │
│                          │ - center-to-edge hub entanglement using two shared parameters (hub_crx, hub_cry)          │
│                          │ - symmetric post-RZ gates mirroring the pre-layer                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design reduces the per-block parameter count (to 11 keys) and emphasizes symmetry,   │
│                          │ which typically improves generalization and speeds up convergence in Adam-driven training │
│                          │ while keeping the problem structure intact. It maintains the same inputs/outputs and      │
│                          │ fixed training loop, data, and feature map.                                               │
