│ patch_name               │ cross_hybrid_crx_crz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Proposed ANSATZ_SPEC crossover: merge the strengths of the two reference seeds by keeping │
│                          │ per-group (corner/edge/center) symmetry-based parameter sharing for pre/post RZ and RY,   │
│                          │ and combining a ring entangler on the outer qubits with a parametric hub entangler that   │
│                          │ uses CRZ gates from center to edges. This keeps the parameter budget modest (11 unique    │
│                          │ per-block parameters, 66 total with 3 uploads and 2 repeats) while enabling a richer      │
│                          │ entangling structure than the baseline and leveraging symmetry-inspired sharing. The ring │
│                          │ uses CRX gates on the outer ring, while the hub uses CRZ gates from the center to edge    │
│                          │ qubits, matching the more promising combination seen in cross-over designs. This should   │
│                          │ improve validation/train dynamics by increasing expressivity without exploding parameter  │
│                          │ count.                                                                                    │
