│ patch_description        │ A fundamentally different, symmetry-aware ansatz that aggressively shares parameters to   │
│                          │ improve generalization while reducing overfitting. This design replaces a purely          │
│                          │ CZ-centric ring with a shared-parameter CRX ring on the outer perimeter, plus hub         │
│                          │ entanglement between the center and edge qubits using a single shared parameter for both  │
│                          │ CRZ and CRX gate types. Pre/post layers still use symmetry-sharing RZ/RY rotations. This  │
│                          │ combination aims to tighten parameter usage (fewer effective degrees of freedom per       │
│                          │ block) while enriching expressivity via simultaneous, parameter-shared multi-gate         │
│                          │ entanglement across the tic-tac-toe board. The result should improve validation accuracy, │
│                          │ reduce train-test gaps, and maintain the same input/output semantics.                     │
