│ patch_name               │ split_crx_ring_params_horizontal_vertical                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce directional CRX ring parameters to increase expressivity while keeping          │
│                          │ adjacency constraints. Split the perimeter CRX gates into horizontal and vertical         │
│                          │ parameter keys (crx_ring_h and crx_ring_v) corresponding to edge orientation. This        │
│                          │ increases the number of trainable parameters per block from 1 to 2 for the ring portion   │
│                          │ (and thus raises N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK), potentially improving the model's ability to        │
│                          │ capture anisotropic correlations on the tic-tac-toe grid. The eight CRX gates around the  │
│                          │ ring are mapped as: (0,1) H, (1,2) H, (2,3) V, (3,4) V, (4,5) H, (5,6) H, (6,7) V, (7,0)  │
│                          │ V. This change adheres to adjacency constraints and keeps the overall architecture        │
│                          │ compatible with the fixed training loop and data handling.                                │
