│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_hub_spoke_ansatz                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of prior performance:                                                            │
│                          │ - Seed (0.57): Hierarchical with CZ ring + CRZ hub (4 params)                             │
│                          │ - Second (0.60): CRX ring (shared) + CRY hub (shared) - better parameter efficiency       │
│                          │ - Current (0.55): Mixed CRZ/CRX hub - underperforming                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second program achieved the best score (0.60) by using:                               │
│                          │ 1. Parametrized ring gates (CRX with single shared parameter) instead of fixed CZ         │
│                          │ 2. Parametrized hub gates (CRY with single shared parameter)                              │
│                          │ 3. This reduced parameter count while maintaining expressivity                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program regressed by mixing CRZ and CRX on the hub, which may create          │
│                          │ interference patterns that hurt learning.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Proposed improvement: Return to the successful CRX ring + CRY hub structure from the      │
│                          │ second program, but add additional single-qubit RX rotations on edges (1,3,5,7) to        │
│                          │ increase expressivity without adding two-qubit gates. This gives edges independent        │
│                          │ rotation axes (RY for general rotation, RX for additional X-basis control) while          │
│                          │ maintaining the efficient parameter sharing on two-qubit gates.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome: Validation accuracy ≥0.65, test accuracy ≥0.50, combined score ≥0.60    │
