│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ compact_shared_ring_hub_ansatz                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This evolved block implements a compact, highly parameter-efficient ansatz with ring CRX  │
│                          │ entanglement and hub CRY entanglement, all sharing a single parameter per motif. By       │
│                          │ reducing per-block parameters from the previous 28+ keys to a fixed 11 unique parameter   │
│                          │ keys (rz_pre_corner/edge/center, ry_corner/edge/center, crx_ring, cry_hub_edge,           │
│                          │ rz_post_corner/edge/center), the total parameter count drops to 66 (3 uploads × 2 repeats │
│                          │ × 11 keys), matching the more performant 60–66 parameter regimes observed in prior seeds. │
│                          │ The design preserves full adjacency constraints (CZ/CNOT around the perimeter;            │
│                          │ center-to-edge hub gates allowed as (8,1),(8,3),(8,5),(8,7)) and maintains symmetry-based │
│                          │ parameter sharing to improve generalization. This approach blends a compact,              │
│                          │ symmetry-aware pre/post-rotation scheme with a lightweight, shared-parameter ring and hub │
│                          │ entanglement, aiming for stronger validation accuracy and reduced train-test gap.         │
