│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_hierarchical_ansatz_with_adaptive_gates                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.55 with validation accuracy of 0.53    │
│                          │ and test accuracy of 0.45. The prior programs showed better performance (0.60 combined    │
│                          │ score with 0.65 validation accuracy).                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of the current ansatz reveals that while it has good parameter sharing (72       │
│                          │ parameters), the hub entanglement layer uses only 2 unique parameters (hub_crx and        │
│                          │ hub_cry) applied to 4 gates. This creates a bottleneck in expressivity.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The improvement strategy:                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Increase the expressivity of the hub entanglement by using 4 independent parameters    │
│                          │ instead of 2 shared ones                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Add an additional layer of single-qubit RX rotations after the ring entanglement to    │
│                          │ provide more fine-grained control                                                         │
│                          │ 3. Maintain the symmetry-inspired structure while allowing more flexibility in the        │
│                          │ center-to-edge coupling                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Increases parameters from 72 to 80 (still reasonable)                                   │
│                          │ - Provides better gradient flow through the hub region                                    │
│                          │ - Allows each edge-to-center connection to learn independently                            │
│                          │ - Maintains the hierarchical structure that was working well in prior versions            │
│                          │ - Balances expressivity with parameter efficiency                                         │
