│ patch_description        │ This redesigns the ANSATZ_SPEC to introduce a CRX ring entangling layer and a centralized │
│                          │ hub entanglement using CRZ/CRX with a single shared parameter. It preserves               │
│                          │ symmetry-based parameter sharing for pre/post RZ and RY layers while replacing the ring   │
│                          │ with CRX gates (shared angle crx_ring) and a unified hub_angle across hub connections.    │
│                          │ This increases expressivity at a controlled parameter budget (11 unique parameters per    │
│                          │ block instead of 10) and maintains adjacency constraints. The overall aim is to improve   │
│                          │ validation/test accuracy and reduce overfitting by leveraging ring-based entanglement and │
│                          │ hub coupling with symmetry, without changing the fixed training loop, data construction,  │
│                          │ or feature map.                                                                           │
