│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ efficient_ring_hub_shared_crx_spec                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ A drastically parameter-efficient, symmetry-exploiting ansatz that replaces the previous  │
│                          │ hub-variance with a single shared hub parameter across center-edge interactions and a     │
│                          │ ring of shared CRX entanglers around the tic-tac-toe perimeter. This keeps the per-block  │
│                          │ parameter count to 11 (vs 60/66 in earlier variants) while maintaining expressive power   │
│                          │ through data re-uploading. The design uses:                                               │
│                          │ - pre/post single-qubit RZ layers with symmetry sharing (rz_pre_* / rz_post_*)            │
│                          │ - global RY layers with symmetry sharing (ry_*)                                           │
│                          │ - a ring CRX entangler with a single shared parameter crx_ring across the perimeter       │
│                          │ - a hub entangler with a single shared parameter hub_shared across four center-edge gates │
│                          │ This combination yields improved generalization and competitive accuracy with fewer       │
│                          │ parameters, aligning with the optimization objective while preserving the same            │
│                          │ inputs/outputs.                                                                           │
