                        Patch Metadata - Gen 57/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_crx_crz_hub_ansatz                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of both prior implementations:                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the inspiration program (score 0.60)**: Uses CRX parametrized ring entanglement │
│                          │ with a single shared parameter across all 8 outer ring edges, and CRY hub entanglement    │
│                          │ from center to edges with one shared parameter. This achieves the highest validation      │
│                          │ accuracy (0.65) and lowest validation loss (2.31).                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the current program (score 0.55)**: Uses per-edge distinct CRZ hub parameters   │
│                          │ (crz_hub_edge_0 through crz_hub_edge_3) which provides more flexibility in center-to-edge │
│                          │ coupling.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Hybrid approach**: Combines CRX ring (shared parameter, more efficient) with         │
│                          │ per-edge CRZ hub parameters (more expressive). This balances:                             │
│                          │    - Parameter efficiency: CRX ring uses 1 parameter instead of 8                         │
│                          │    - Hub expressiveness: Per-edge CRZ parameters (4 params) vs shared CRY (1 param)       │
│                          │    - Total params: 11 per block (vs 12 in inspiration, 13 in current)                     │
│                          │    - Better generalization: Reduces overfitting by using fewer total parameters while     │
│                          │ maintaining hub flexibility                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hybrid structure is:                                                                  │
│                          │ - Pre-entanglement RZ (3 params: corners, edges, center)                                  │
│                          │ - RY rotations (3 params: corners, edges, center)                                         │
│                          │ - Ring CRX entanglement (1 shared param across all 8 edges)                               │
│                          │ - Hub CRZ entanglement (4 distinct params for center-to-edge)                             │
│                          │ - Post-entanglement RZ (3 params: corners, edges, center)                                 │
│                          │ = 14 params per block × 3 uploads × 2 repeats = 84 total params                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve validation accuracy while maintaining good generalization.            │
