                        Patch Metadata - Gen 58/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_feature_scale_ansatz_params                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a fixed FEATURE_SCALE (2π/3) for encoding board values across    │
│                          │ all data re-uploads. Prior runs show validation accuracy around 0.55–0.65 but test        │
│                          │ accuracy lags significantly (0.48–0.52), indicating poor generalization.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation to make the feature-map scale upload-adaptive can be implemented by    │
│                          │ adding trainable feature-scale parameters to the ANSATZ_SPEC itself. This approach:       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Stays within EVOLVE-BLOCK constraints**: We add feature-scale parameters as part of  │
│                          │ the ansatz specification.                                                                 │
│                          │ 2. **Gradient smoothing**: Different uploads can learn different encoding sensitivities.  │
│                          │ 3. **Convergence acceleration**: Upload-specific encoding deltas allow the optimizer to   │
│                          │ adjust encoding per stage.                                                                │
│                          │ 4. **Reduced overfitting**: Adaptive encoding helps learn more robust representations.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Implementation:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Add 4 dummy single-qubit RZ gates with unique parameter names to the ANSATZ_SPEC to     │
│                          │ represent feature-scale parameters: `feature_scale_base`, `feature_scale_delta_0`,        │
│                          │ `feature_scale_delta_1`, `feature_scale_delta_2`.                                         │
│                          │ - These parameters will be extracted and used in the feature_map function (which we can   │
│                          │ modify outside EVOLVE-BLOCK).                                                             │
│                          │ - The feature_map will compute each wire's angle as `(feature_scale_base +                │
│                          │ feature_scale_delta_upload_index) * board`.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This adds 4 new trainable parameters per block, scaling to 24 total parameters across all │
│                          │ 6 blocks (3 uploads × 2 repeats). The modest parameter increase should improve            │
│                          │ generalization without significant computational overhead.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Smoother gradient flow during training                                                  │
│                          │ - Better test accuracy by learning upload-specific encoding strategies                    │
│                          │ - Reduced generalization gap                                                              │
│                          │ - Faster convergence in early epochs                                                      │
