│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lean_shared_prepost_hierarchical                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite uses aggressive parameter sharing by tying pre- and post-entanglement RZ     │
│                          │ gates to the same per-wire class parameters (rz_corner, rz_edge, rz_center). It also      │
│                          │ keeps shared RY parameters (ry_corner, ry_edge, ry_center) and a shared hub parameter     │
│                          │ (hub_angle) across CRZ and CRX on center-to-edge connections. The result is a leaner      │
│                          │ per-block parameter count (7 keys instead of 10), reducing overfitting and train-time,    │
│                          │ while preserving expressive power through layer-wise RY/RZ and CZCRZ/CRX interactions.    │
│                          │ This should improve validation/test performance and reduce generalization gap with fewer  │
│                          │ parameters and similar or better train efficiency.                                        │
