│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_param_block_5param                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Redesign the ANSATZ_SPEC to aggressively share parameters across the entire per-block     │
│                          │ layout. This reduces the parameter budget per block from 11+ keys (66 total) to 5 unique  │
│                          │ keys, yielding 30 total trainable parameters (5 keys × 3 uploads × 2 repeats). The        │
│                          │ structure maintains the same data flow and outputs, but increases parameter efficiency    │
│                          │ and enforces stronger symmetry by sharing pre/post rotations across all wires, while      │
│                          │ preserving the ring (CRY) and hub (CRX) entangling motifs. The gating remains within the  │
│                          │ allowed edge-adjacent connectivity, and the overall depth and gate count are reduced      │
│                          │ without changing the fixed training loop or feature map semantics.                        │
