│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ crx_ring_cry_hub_hybrid                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This cross-over merges the strongest elements from the two reference implementations by   │
│                          │ adopting a hybrid ansatz that uses:                                                       │
│                          │ - Pre- and post-entanglement RZ gates with per-group parameter sharing (corners, edges,   │
│                          │ center) to leverage tic-tac-toe symmetry.                                                 │
│                          │ - RY rotations per group (corners, edges, center) for expressive but compact single-qubit │
│                          │ rotations.                                                                                │
│                          │ - A parametrized CRX ring around the outer 8 qubits (shared parameter crx_ring) for       │
│                          │ efficient entangling structure.                                                           │
│                          │ - Hub entanglement using CRY gates from the center to the edge qubits, with a single      │
│                          │ shared parameter cry_hub_edge.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design preserves the original inputs/outputs and maintains the same parameter budget │
│                          │ (66 parameters) as the prior best-performing setup, while introducing the CRY hub-edge    │
│                          │ entanglement and keeping the CRX ring. The approach aims to reduce trainable parameters   │
│                          │ while improving validation performance and generalization, aligning with the crossover    │
│                          │ strategy to enhance the overall score. The rest of the training loop, data construction,  │
│                          │ measurements, and evaluation remain unchanged.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All changes are localized inside the EVOLVE-BLOCK and specifically modify the ANSATZ_SPEC │
│                          │ generation to implement the cross-over structure.                                         │
