╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_ry2_layer_after_hub                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.57 with 66 parameters. The prior       │
│                          │ programs show that:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. The first program (60 params, score 0.57) used CZ fixed gates with CRZ hub             │
│                          │ entanglement                                                                              │
│                          │ 2. The second program (66 params, score 0.60) used CRX ring with CRY hub entanglement,    │
│                          │ achieving the best score                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. The current program (66 params, score 0.57) uses CRY ring with CRX hub entanglement,   │
│                          │ but underperforms                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests inserting a second RY rotation layer between the hub          │
│                          │ entanglement and post-entanglement RZ. This layer would:                                  │
│                          │ - Add 3 new shared parameters: "ry2_corner", "ry2_edge", "ry2_center"                     │
│                          │ - Apply RY rotations to all 9 qubits after the hub entanglement                           │
│                          │ - Capture nonlinear effects introduced by the hub entanglers                              │
│                          │ - Increase expressivity with minimal parameter overhead (only 3 params per block)         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach is inspired by the observation that the best-performing program (score      │
│                          │ 0.60) had more structured entanglement. Adding a second RY layer provides an additional   │
│                          │ degree of freedom for the optimizer to refine the quantum state after hub entanglement,   │
│                          │ similar to how intermediate rotations in EfficientSU2 improve expressivity.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The total parameters would increase from 66 to 72 (3 new params × 3 uploads × 2 repeats), │
│                          │ which is still reasonable and follows the pattern of successful VQC designs that use      │
│                          │ multiple rotation layers.                                                                 │
