│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ tic_tac_toe_crossover_ansatz                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Proposes a crossover-inspired ANSATZ_SPEC that blends the best parts of the two prior     │
│                          │ implementations. The new spec uses:                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Layer 1 and Layer 2: symmetry-aware pre-rotations (RZ/RY) with per-group parameter      │
│                          │ sharing (corners, edges, center).                                                         │
│                          │ - Layer 3: ring entanglement with a single shared CRX parameter around the outer          │
│                          │ perimeter (crx_ring).                                                                     │
│                          │ - Layer 4: hub entanglement between the center and edge qubits using CRY with a single    │
│                          │ shared parameter (cry_hub_edge).                                                          │
│                          │ - Layer 5: post-entanglement RZ rotations with per-group sharing (rz_post_corner,         │
│                          │ rz_post_edge, rz_post_center).                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This structure mirrors the crossover between the "ring CRX + hub CRY" idea and the        │
│                          │ original symmetry-based layout, reducing parameter count while preserving expressive      │
│                          │ power. It maintains the same inputs/outputs, gates, and connectivity rules as the fixed   │
│                          │ training framework, and fits the required EVOLVE-BLOCK constraints.                       │
