╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_ry2_ring_cry_hub                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Proposed enhanced ansatz for a 9-qubit tic-tac-toe QML classifier.                        │
│                          │ Key changes inside the EVOLVE-BLOCK ANSATZ_SPEC:                                          │
│                          │ - Layer 3: Ring entanglement on the outer loop uses CRX with a single shared parameter    │
│                          │ crx_ring across all ring edges, increasing expressivity with a compact parameter budget.  │
│                          │ - Layer 4: Hub entanglement uses CRY between center (8) and each edge (1,3,5,7) with a    │
│                          │ single shared parameter cry_hub_edge for symmetry-driven efficiency.                      │
│                          │ - Layer 5: Inserted a second, symmetry-consistent RY layer (ry2_corner, ry2_edge,         │
│                          │ ry2_center) after hub entanglement and before post-entanglement RZ, increasing            │
│                          │ nonlinearity without exploding parameter counts.                                          │
│                          │ - Layer 6: Post-entanglement RZ rotations remain, but now follow the added ry2 layer to   │
│                          │ complete the enhanced expressive motif.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - The added ry2 layer captures richer nonlinear mixing after hub entanglement, aligned    │
│                          │ with the suggested motif for improved validation/test performance.                        │
│                          │ - The CRX ring with a shared parameter crx_ring adds a cohesive perimeter entangling      │
│                          │ mechanism while keeping parameter count modest.                                           │
│                          │ - The cry_hub_edge layering provides center-to-edge coupling with symmetry, balancing     │
│                          │ expressivity and parameter efficiency.                                                    │
