│ patch_name               │ ring_reinforcement_crx_ring                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a ring reinforcement by replacing the CZ-only ring with a two-pass CRX ring     │
│                          │ around the tic-tac-toe perimeter. All ring gates share a single parameter crx_ring to     │
│                          │ keep the parameter count stable (one additional parameter beyond the baseline, but we     │
│                          │ maintain a similar total block depth growth). The first pass executes CRX gates in        │
│                          │ forward order around the ring; the second pass executes the same gates in reverse order.  │
│                          │ This deepens entanglement with minimal parameter overhead and can improve expressivity    │
│                          │ and generalization, potentially raising validation/test performance and narrowing         │
│                          │ train-test gaps on the tic-tac-toe task.                                                  │
