                        Patch Metadata - Gen 74/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ edge_orientation_symmetry_refinement                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 84 parameters and a score of 0.56, while the second prior program │
│                          │ with 66 parameters achieved 0.60. The current design has redundant entanglement (both CZ  │
│                          │ and CRX on the same ring edges, plus duplicate hub connections) leading to parameter      │
│                          │ bloat and overfitting without improved expressivity.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests subdividing edge symmetry into horizontal and vertical        │
│                          │ subgroups while preserving parameter efficiency. This approach:                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Reduces parameter count** from 84 to 66 by eliminating redundant gates and merging   │
│                          │ center parameters                                                                         │
│                          │ 2. **Adds directional sensitivity** by distinguishing horizontal edges (1,5) from         │
│                          │ vertical edges (3,7) in pre/post RZ layers                                                │
│                          │ 3. **Maintains the five-layer motif** that proved effective in prior work                 │
│                          │ 4. **Keeps depth ~70** by removing duplicate ring entanglement                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that tic-tac-toe has natural horizontal/vertical structure             │
│                          │ (rows/columns/diagonals), so giving the circuit finer edge-orientation sensitivity while  │
│                          │ keeping total parameters at 66 should improve generalization and reduce the train-test    │
│                          │ gap.                                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Changes:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Replace redundant CZ + CRX ring with a single CRX ring (shared parameter)               │
│                          │ - Remove duplicate hub connections                                                        │
│                          │ - Split edge parameters into horizontal (1,5) and vertical (3,7) variants for pre/post RZ │
│                          │ - Merge pre_center and post_center into single rz_center parameter                        │
│                          │ - Use distinct CRX parameters for hub edges (4 parameters instead of 1 shared)            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves the 66-parameter budget while adding structural sensitivity to board       │
│                          │ geometry.                                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
