│ patch_description        │ Inspired by prior ShinkaEvolve tic-tac-toe ansatz seeds, this design keeps a              │
│                          │ symmetry-guided, parameter-efficient structure while enriching the entangling pattern     │
│                          │ without increasing the number of trainable parameters. The key change is a two-pass CRX   │
│                          │ ring entangler on the board perimeter (same shared angle) with ascending and descending   │
│                          │ edge orders, which diversifies the entanglement without adding new parameters. This is    │
│                          │ complemented by a center-to-edge hub entangler (CRY) and the same pre/post RZ/RY          │
│                          │ scaffolding as before. By reusing a single CRX parameter across two ring traversals, we   │
│                          │ increase circuit expressivity and potential performance while maintaining parameter       │
│                          │ efficiency. The overall parameter count per block remains the same (no extra learnable    │
│                          │ parameters were introduced), so parameter_efficiency remains interpretable while          │
│                          │ potentially improving validation/test metrics through richer entanglement patterns.       │
