                        Patch Metadata - Gen 80/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_modality_ansatz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This redesigned program improves upon the current hybrid ansatz by introducing adaptive   │
│                          │ entanglement modality switching. The key structural innovation is to make the ring and    │
│                          │ hub entanglement layers dynamically select between different gate types (CRX, CRY, CRZ)   │
│                          │ based on the block repetition index, without adding parameters.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Structural improvements:**                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Adaptive Ring Entanglement**: Instead of using only CRX for all ring gates, the ring │
│                          │ layer alternates between CRX and CRY gates based on `block_index % 2`. This allows the    │
│                          │ circuit to explore complementary correlation patterns (X-axis vs Y-axis rotations) across │
│                          │ different data re-uploads, capturing richer entanglement structures.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Adaptive Hub Entanglement**: Similarly, hub gates alternate between CRY and CRZ      │
│                          │ based on `block_index % 2`, providing diverse center-to-edge coupling mechanisms.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Unified Parameter Sharing**: Both ring and hub layers continue to share single       │
│                          │ parameters across their respective gates, maintaining parameter efficiency (66 params     │
│                          │ total, same as current).                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Modular Gate Application**: The `apply_ansatz_block` function is enhanced with a     │
│                          │ helper function to conditionally select gate types, making the logic clearer and more     │
│                          │ maintainable.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected benefits:**                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - **Improved test accuracy**: Alternating entanglement modalities can help the circuit    │
│                          │ learn more complex decision boundaries by exploring different quantum correlations.       │
│                          │ - **Better generalization**: The diversity in entanglement patterns across re-uploads may │
│                          │ reduce overfitting by preventing the circuit from settling into a single local minimum.   │
│                          │ - **Maintained efficiency**: No additional parameters are added; the same 66 parameters   │
│                          │ are used more effectively through structural diversity.                                   │
│                          │ - **Reduced validation loss**: The richer entanglement landscape should lead to better    │
│                          │ optimization trajectories.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach combines the best aspects of prior programs (parametrized ring from program │
│                          │ 2, shared hub from program 1) while adding a new dimension of expressivity through        │
│                          │ gate-type modulation.                                                                     │
