│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tic_tac_toe_symm60_param_ansatz                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ A compact, highly symmetric hierarchical variational ansatz with deliberate parameter     │
│                          │ sharing to reduce the parameter count to 60 per full block (and 60 total after accounting │
│                          │ for uploads/repeats). The design preserves the Tic-Tac-Toe grid symmetry and uses:        │
│                          │ - Pre- and post- entanglement RZ layers with corner/edge/center groups                    │
│                          │ - Shared RY layers across corners/edges/center                                            │
│                          │ - Ring CZ entanglement on the outer perimeter                                             │
│                          │ - Ring CRX entanglement with a single shared parameter across the ring                    │
│                          │ - Center-to-edge hub entanglement with a single shared parameter across hub edges         │
│                          │ Crucially, the center parameters are shared between pre and post layers (rz_center),      │
│                          │ reducing duplication and enabling a stronger second-repeat amplitude control. This        │
│                          │ structure aims to reduce depth and total parameters while maintaining expressive power,   │
│                          │ improving validation/test accuracy and reducing train-test gap relative to the previous   │
│                          │ designs.                                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
