│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_hub_crx_plus_cz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This proposal keeps the same overall parameter budget as the prior best-performing        │
│                          │ variant (66 parameters total for the full run with 3 uploads and 2 repeats, i.e., 11      │
│                          │ parameters per block), but increases expressive power by restructuring the entangling     │
│                          │ layers. Specifically:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Layer 3 (ring entanglement) uses a ring of CRX gates around the outer 8 qubits with a   │
│                          │ single shared parameter crx_ring, increasing depth without adding trainable parameters.   │
│                          │ - Layer 4 (hub entanglement) uses center-to-edge CRY gates with a single shared parameter │
│                          │ cry_hub_edge, and adds center-to-edge CZ gates to deepen entanglement without adding      │
│                          │ parameters.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Layer 1 (pre-entanglement) and Layer 2 (RY) keep parameter sharing across symmetry      │
│                          │ classes (corners, edges, center) as in the prior designs.                                 │
│                          │ - Layer 5 (post-entanglement) maintains symmetry-driven parameter sharing across          │
│                          │ corner/edge/center with rz_post_corner, rz_post_edge, rz_post_center.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design preserves the fixed training loop, data construction, feature map,            │
│                          │ re-uploading strategy, and measurement scheme, while boosting circuit depth and           │
│                          │ expressivity through a deeper fixed topology that leverages parameter sharing for         │
│                          │ efficiency. The goal is to improve validation/test performance and reduce generalization  │
│                          │ gap without inflating the parameter count.                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0044                                                                                   │
