│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_parametrized_ring_with_hub                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of prior programs shows:                                                         │
│                          │ - Program 1 (score 0.57): CZ ring + CRZ hub → validation 0.60, test 0.48                  │
│                          │ - Program 2 (score 0.60): CRX ring (shared param) + CRY hub (shared param) → validation   │
│                          │ 0.65, test 0.50                                                                           │
│                          │ - Current (score 0.55): CZ ring + mixed CRZ/CRX hub → validation 0.53, test 0.47          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Program 2's approach of using parametrized gates with aggressive parameter sharing on     │
│                          │ both ring and hub significantly outperforms the others. The current program regressed by  │
│                          │ reverting to fixed CZ gates on the ring.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Strategy:**                                                                             │
│                          │ Return to the proven structure of program 2 (parametrized CRX ring + CRY hub) which       │
│                          │ achieved the best validation accuracy (0.65). This structure:                             │
│                          │ 1. Uses a single shared "crx_ring" parameter for all 8 ring edges (CRX gates)             │
│                          │ 2. Uses a single shared "cry_hub_edge" parameter for all 4 hub edges (CRY gates)          │
│                          │ 3. Maintains aggressive parameter sharing for efficiency and regularization               │
│                          │ 4. Keeps the same symmetric pre/post RZ layers                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is the most direct path to improving performance based on empirical evidence from    │
│                          │ the prior runs.                                                                           │
