│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ alternate_ring_entanglement_axes                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a single CRX gate with shared parameter `crx_ring` for all eight │
│                          │ edges around the perimeter. While parameter sharing improves efficiency, it may limit the │
│                          │ expressivity of the ring entanglement layer.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests alternating between CRX and CRY on the eight outer edges:     │
│                          │ - CRX on (0,1), CRY on (1,2), CRX on (2,3), CRY on (3,4), CRX on (4,5), CRY on (5,6), CRX │
│                          │ on (6,7), CRY on (7,0)                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All eight gates still draw from a single shared parameter key `crx_ring`, maintaining the │
│                          │ 66-parameter budget. By mixing two-qubit rotation axes around the perimeter, we diversify │
│                          │ the nonlocal correlations without increasing the parameter count. This leverages the      │
│                          │ board's 4-fold rotational symmetry while introducing richer entanglement patterns that    │
│                          │ may help the circuit learn more complex decision boundaries for the tic-tac-toe           │
│                          │ classification task.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The alternating pattern respects the grid topology and should improve validation accuracy │
│                          │ and reduce the generalization gap by providing more flexible entanglement without         │
│                          │ overfitting.                                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0315                                                                                   │
