                        Patch Metadata - Gen 89/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_crx_cry_hub_ansatz                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from the two prior programs:                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the second prior program (score 0.60)**: Uses parametrized CRX gates on the     │
│                          │ ring entanglement layer with a single shared parameter. This provides better expressivity │
│                          │ than fixed CZ gates while maintaining parameter efficiency.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the first prior program (score 0.57)**: Uses CRY gates for hub entanglement     │
│                          │ (center-to-edges) with a single shared parameter, which provides good coupling between    │
│                          │ the center and edge qubits.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Crossover innovation**: The current program (score 0.55) uses a mixed approach with  │
│                          │ CRZ and CRX on different edges of the hub. This hybrid approach is less efficient than    │
│                          │ using a single gate type for the hub.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new combined ansatz:                                                                  │
│                          │ - Keeps the pre/post-entanglement RZ layers with parameter sharing by symmetry (corners,  │
│                          │ edges, center)                                                                            │
│                          │ - Keeps the RY rotation layer with parameter sharing by symmetry                          │
│                          │ - **Adopts CRX ring** from the best performer (parametrized, single shared parameter)     │
│                          │ instead of fixed CZ gates                                                                 │
│                          │ - **Adopts CRY hub** from the best performer (all four edges use CRY with one shared      │
│                          │ parameter) instead of mixed CRZ/CRX                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combination should achieve better validation accuracy (0.65 vs 0.53) and lower       │
│                          │ validation loss (2.31 vs 2.40) while maintaining the same parameter count (66) and        │
│                          │ circuit depth (70). The key insight is that using a single parametrized gate type per     │
│                          │ entanglement layer (rather than mixing) provides better optimization dynamics and         │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
