│ patch_description        │ Proposed cross-over: merge the symmetry-driven hierarchical base (pre/post RZ and RY      │
│                          │ layers) with a ring-based entanglement motif using CRX on the outer ring, followed by hub │
│                          │ entanglement using CRY from the center to edge qubits. This combines the best aspects     │
│                          │ observed in the two reference implementations: symmetry-aware parameter sharing           │
│                          │ (efficiency) and a richer, cross-architecture entanglement pattern (potentially improving │
│                          │ validation/test performance). The ansatz still respects the adjacency constraints and     │
│                          │ reuses shared parameters across the ring and hub gates to maintain a compact              │
│                          │ parameterization. The resulting ANSATZ_SPEC should yield improved generalization while    │
│                          │ keeping the same input/output behavior as the original program.                           │
