│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_ring_hub_ring_improved                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Proposes a reorganized, more entangled ansatz within a single block by splitting the      │
│                          │ perimeter CRX ring into two segments with a hub CRY layer in between. This                │
│                          │ “ring–hub–ring” arrangement preserves parameter efficiency (same 11 unique block          │
│                          │ parameters), depth, and connectivity constraints, but enhances entanglement mixing across │
│                          │ the tic-tac-toe qubit layout. It interleaves a four-edge CRX ring, a CRY hub connecting   │
│                          │ the center to edge qubits, and then the remaining four CRX ring edges, followed by        │
│                          │ post-entanglement RZ rotations. This structure aims to improve validation/test accuracy   │
│                          │ and reduce train-test gap while preserving the fixed training loop, data construction,    │
│                          │ measurements, and overall block semantics (N_UPLOADS=3, N_REPEATS=2, feature map as       │
│                          │ specified, and per-block parameter sharing).                                              │
