│ patch_description        │ This rewrite updates the EVOLVE-BLOCKANZSATZ_SPEC to improve expressivity and efficiency  │
│                          │ by altering the internal ansatz composition while preserving the fixed training loop,     │
│                          │ data, feature map, and metrics pipeline.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Layer 3 ring entanglement uses CRX gates around the outer ring with a single shared     │
│                          │ parameter crx_ring (8 gates share one parameter).                                         │
│                          │ - Layer 4 hub entanglement uses CRY gates from center to edges (1,3,5,7) with a single    │
│                          │ shared parameter cry_hub_edge (all hub-edge gates share one parameter).                   │
│                          │ - Layer 1 (pre-rotations), Layer 2 (rotations), and Layer 5 (post-rotations) continue to  │
│                          │ use symmetry-sharing style parameterization, preserving parameter efficiency and the      │
│                          │ original symmetry-inspired motifs.                                                        │
│                          │ - Total parameters per block become 11, yielding N_PARAMS = 11 * N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS =  │
│                          │ 66, consistent with a known more expressive configuration that previously achieved higher │
│                          │ scores.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The resulting ANSATZ_SPEC remains compatible with the existing validation and mapping     │
│                          │ logic, and the overall program continues to produce the same inputs/outputs required by   │
│                          │ the fixed training loop and evaluation pipeline.                                          │
