│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ tic_tac_toe_hybrid_ansatz                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Cross-over hybrid ansatz: combine the best-performing ring and hub entanglements from the │
│                          │ two reference implementations. The ring uses parameterized CRX gates around the outer     │
│                          │ ring (shared parameter crx_ring), while the hub-layer combines CRZ and CRY gates from     │
│                          │ center to each edge with shared parameters (crz_hub_edge and cry_hub_edge). This          │
│                          │ preserves parameter sharing for efficiency and adheres to adjacency constraints. All      │
│                          │ other layers (pre/post RZ and RY with symmetry-based sharing) remain as in the original   │
│                          │ seeds. The resulting ANSATZ_SPEC is richer than the baseline, potentially improving       │
│                          │ validation accuracy while keeping the same training loop, data, and measurement           │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
