│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crx_ring_interleaved_hub_cry                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Proposes a parameter-efficient, interleaved CRX ring plus hub CRY ansatz block.           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Split the CRX ring into two interleaved halves (0-1,1-2,2-3,3-4) and (4-5,5-6,6-7,7-0). │
│                          │ - Sandwiched CRY hub gates (center-edge) between the two CRX halves.                      │
│                          │ - Reuse the same CRX parameter across both ring halves to minimize parameters (crx_ring). │
│                          │ - Use a single hub parameter (cry_hub_edge) shared across all four center-to-edge CRY     │
│                          │ gates.                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Preserve symmetry-based pre/post-RZ and RY layers to retain the existing structured     │
│                          │ inductive bias.                                                                           │
│                          │ - All gates respect the adjacency constraints of GRID_EDGE_SET.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected benefits:                                                                        │
│                          │ - Reduced parameter count (per-block) compared to previous designs, improving sample      │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Richer two-qubit mixing via CRX–CRY–CRX sequencing, improving expressive power without  │
│                          │ bloating the parameter space.                                                             │
│                          │ - Better generalization and faster convergence for Adam optimization under fixed          │
│                          │ data/training loop.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new ANSATZ_SPEC is implemented inside the EVOLVE-BLOCK by redefining                  │
│                          │ _build_hierarchical_ansatz_spec.                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
