                        Patch Metadata - Gen 98/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ interleaved_crx_cry_ring                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 78 parameters (per-edge CRX hub gates) but achieves only 0.55     │
│                          │ combined score with 0.47 test accuracy. The prior program with 66 parameters (shared CRY  │
│                          │ hub gates) achieved 0.60 combined score with 0.50 test accuracy.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests splitting the CRX ring into two interleaved groups and        │
│                          │ sandwiching CRY hub gates between them. This creates a CRX–CRY–CRX mixing pattern per     │
│                          │ block that:                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Reduces parameters**: Uses only 2 shared parameters (crx_ring and cry_hub_edge)      │
│                          │ instead of 4 distinct hub parameters, bringing us to 60 parameters per block (same as the │
│                          │ best prior).                                                                              │
│                          │ 2. **Increases two-qubit mixing depth**: Interleaving CRX and CRY gates creates richer    │
│                          │ entanglement patterns without adding many gates.                                          │
│                          │ 3. **Improves expressivity**: The CRX–CRY–CRX sandwich allows different rotation axes to  │
│                          │ interact, potentially capturing more complex decision boundaries.                         │
│                          │ 4. **Maintains connectivity**: All gates respect the grid edge constraints.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The structure becomes:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Layer 1: Pre-entanglement RZ (shared)                                                   │
│                          │ - Layer 2: RY rotations (shared)                                                          │
│                          │ - Layer 3a: CRX on first half of ring edges (0–1, 1–2, 2–3, 3–4) with shared parameter    │
│                          │ - Layer 3b: CRY hub gates (8–1, 8–3, 8–5, 8–7) with shared parameter                      │
│                          │ - Layer 3c: CRX on second half of ring edges (4–5, 5–6, 6–7, 7–0) with shared parameter   │
│                          │ - Layer 4: Post-entanglement RZ (shared)                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces the parameter count from 78 to 60 per block (matching the best prior) while  │
│                          │ increasing circuit depth and two-qubit gate mixing, which should improve generalization   │
│                          │ and test accuracy.                                                                        │
