│ patch_name               │ add-mid-ry-and-merge-rz-keys                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a mid-block RY layer and merge corner/edge pre/post RZ keys into shared keys to │
│                          │ increase expressivity while reducing parameter duplication. Specifically:                 │
│                          │ - Merge rz_pre_corner/rz_post_corner into a single rz_corner and rz_pre_edge/rz_post_edge │
│                          │ into rz_edge (center keys unchanged).                                                     │
│                          │ - Add a new mid-block RY layer before the CRX ring with new keys: ry_mid_corner,          │
│                          │ ry_mid_edge, ry_mid_center.                                                               │
│                          │ - Maintain existing ry_corner/ry_edge/ry_center for the initial RY layer and keep         │
│                          │ crx_ring and crz_hub_edge as shared per-block parameters.                                 │
│                          │ - Post-entanglement RZ continues to share rz_corner/rz_edge for corners/edges and         │
│                          │ rz_post_center for the center.                                                            │
│                          │ This increases the parameter count per block to 12 (72 total), potentially improving      │
│                          │ expressivity and validation performance while preserving symmetry benefits. Ensure        │
│                          │ ANSATZ_SPEC reflects these new keys and ordering.                                         │
